/-!
# Kill data for the level-60 tail sector (generated; not hand-written)

`killChunks` holds the kill divisors of the 18,742 Jacobi-inconclusive pools, in enumeration order (`0` = no divisor
found), packed 128 bits each, 1000 per chunk. `survivorChunks` holds the 3,698 pools without a kill, packed 16 bits per
prime, 20 primes per pool, 500 pools per chunk. Both come from `code/hunt/survivor_kill.rs` (8-shard run, 2026-10-17).
Nothing here is trusted: the check re-verifies every divisor (`checkAll`), and a wrong entry makes that check fail.

Paper: Proposition `prop:tailkill`.
-/

